  "rule": "Rhythm rule, fixed before the comparison. Real windows: validation split of the six original datasets and the three PTT contexts, intervals from the repaired PPG peaks (flow.window_peaks), windows with >= 10 intervals. Each window is commanded with its own mean rate and the 5th-95th percentiles of its instantaneous rate; R0 and R1 each generate one interval sequence per window (seed 20261021) of the same length. Features: lag-1 and lag-2 autocorrelation of the intervals and RMSSD/SDNN, each scored as the Wasserstein-1 distance between generated and real values divided by the real interquartile range, and the range term, the mean of |ln(achieved 5th-95th percentile rate width / commanded width)|. Score per dataset: mean of the four terms; overall score: mean over datasets. R1 replaces R0 if its overall score is lower than R0's by more than 20% and its mean absolute error of the mean rate is <= 1 bpm. Guard for the deployed generators: with the chosen model encoded into z, the PhysioFlow and PhysioMix strips must keep a mean rate error <= 1 bpm against the command on the same windows.",
